WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.400
To get our eyes tested

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.400
we’ve always had to go to an optometrist,

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.220
and that can be a pain.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:07.820
But now, maybe we don’t have to go!

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.800
Is it the quick and cheap alternative

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.800
that you’ve been looking for?

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.700
Welcome to your online eye exam

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.540
A company called Opternative,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.260
as in optometry alternative,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.220
claims it has a new online eye exam

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.980
that’s as good as an in-person exam.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.680
We’ll measure how clearly you see.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.360
Take 11 heel to toe steps away from your computer.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.000
Gently cover your left eye

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.740
and press the button to begin.

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.800
It’s hard to believe that this could replicate

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.680
what optometrists do.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.760
But the author of the book “Bottleneckers”

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.940
who researched this exam says it is just as

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:44.720
good as an in person exam.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.720
At least as good, and sometimes better

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:47.680
some research has indicated.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.020
How can it be better?

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:49.860
It’s over the internet?

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.680
This is the beauty of technology.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.100
Select the square with the sharper lines.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.480
You look at the computer

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.920
while following instructions on your cell phone.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.840
Optometrist Steven Lee founded Opternative.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.760
In this TED talk he explains that he did it because

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.520
a patient complained about how difficult

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.920
it was to get to his office.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.440
She’d skip work and waste most of her day

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.400
to spend just a few minutes with me.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.760
That’s when she stopped me.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:16.160
She said: “Doctor Lee,

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:18.000
why can’t we just do this at home?”

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.320
So he invented a way to do that.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.680
Select which character looks different.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.440
All you need is a computer and a smart phone.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.240
That’s it.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.600
This is really foolhardy and really dangerous.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.040
The American optometric association says

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.840
a home test is unacceptably risky because

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.200
no optometrist is there to look for diseases.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.480
So I said to the company spokesman:

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.880
Sick people are not going to be diagnosed.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.920
Sick people are not allowed to take the exam.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.160
Well how do you stop them, you ask them questions?

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.200
Absolutely.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.120
Just like would be done in your optometrist’s office.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.000
Optometrist is not going to be able

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.360
to screen you for diabetes.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:55.520
They can’t take a blood test.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.080
The Opternative computer program

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.920
does ask you medical questions.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.440
If the program suspects that you have disease,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.440
the company won’t give you a prescription.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.200
It refers you to an eye doctor.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.960
It is a tool that allows you to take a test or be screened.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.240
Those results are then reviewed by

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.720
a licensed ophthalmologist.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.920
Not good enough, says the Optometric Association.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.120
They want to force everyone to go to an eye doctor.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:21.200
They’re the bottlenecker here

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.280
and they’ve persuaded 13 states to draft bills

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.400
banning at home tests.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.880
Groups of doctors that basically said,

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.400
patients like yourself should not have the right to

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.520
make any choices in your vision care.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.240
Bottleneckers like the optometrists have clout

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.440
in the legislatures, because they give the

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:40.120
politicians money.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.880
When South Carolina’s legislature

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.320
banned the at-home test,

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.160
then Gov Nikki Haley spoke up

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.240
for the patients.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.680
She vetoed the ban.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.480
She said it was anti-competitive.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.840
And it is!

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.480
But the legislature were so beholden

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:54.880
to the optometrists

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.640
that they overrode her veto.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.320
It’s as if car makers got together and

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.720
got laws passed forcing all of us

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.120
to buy the most expensive cars.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.960
But often consumers don’t want all Cadillacs,

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.080
sometimes they are satisfied with a Chevrolet.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.840
Many Americans never visit any eye doctor.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.360
This test at least gives all of us a choice.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.920
What is right,

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.440
forbidding a person from seeing

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.480
unless they first allow you to invasively

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.760
test their eyes?

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.840
Please hold your phone

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.400
at a normal reading distance.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.760
I didn’t have to go through an invasive test.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:31.160
Your prescription is in sight.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.360
In a few days I got this prescription,

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.120
which turned out to be the same prescription I get

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.760
from my expensive eye doctor.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.720
And I paid just $50.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.840
On average optometrists in my town charge $95.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:45.280
It’s good to have a choice.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:47.560
These glasses were the correct prescription,

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:49.200
for less money.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.320
The optometry lobby

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.280
doesn’t want us to have that choice?

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.160
No, they don’t!

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.360
Bottleneckers make life worse for you.

